WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Democrats hold 56 Senate seats after Mary Peltola wins Alaska. This is Omni View, episode 240. After that result, Trump is on the ground in Shenzhen with a split among Ukraine's allies. Brussels has put a loan on the table for Kiev, and crowds in Porto Prince turned out for foreign troops. Mary Peltola, a Democrat, has taken Alaska's Senate seat from two-term Republican Dan Sullivan. Al Jazeera, citing the Associated Press, puts her at 50.1%

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.420
1% of first choice votes to his 45.8, with about 99% counted.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.780
The BBC says that confirmation caps the Democrats route in the midterm Senate races.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.860
It is the party's first Senate win in Alaska in more than a decade.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:50.320
Alaska uses ranked choice voting, which means a majority of first choice votes elect someone

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.820
outright, and no later rounds are counted.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.700
Peltola is Yepic.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:59.720
She became the first Alaska native in Congress by winning a special election for the state's

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:07.680
only house seat in 2022, served until January 2025 and lost that seat in 2024. A second

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:12.900
man, retired teacher Daniel J. Sullivan, stood with no party label beside the incumbent,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:18.400
listed as Dan S. Sullivan. In June, the state elections division took the teacher off

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.420
the ballot, saying the name was chosen to confuse voters and noting a consultant who had worked

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:29.240
for Peltola. A superior court judge put him back, and the Alaska Supreme Court agreed on June

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:34.860
29th. The Trump administration alleged that Peltola's campaign recruited that second Sullivan

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:40.900
on purpose, a tactic called ballot stacking, to split Republican votes. Al Jazeera reports

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:46.300
that even if every namesake vote had gone to the senator, he still would have lost. Scott

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:51.740
Lucas of University College Dublin's Clinton Institute told Al Jazeera she campaigned as

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:57.200
a pragmatist on energy jobs, the border and guns, and played down the Democratic label,

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.920
while Sullivan carried the cost of Trump's ticket.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.460
The administration's charge is that a look-alike name was a decoy, and that the old consultant

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:08.000
link shows it was not a random, independent bid.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.120
The record the courts and the count produced is different.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.040
Judges said the teacher could stay on the ballot, and the tally al-Jazeera sites from the

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.100
Associated Press shows those extra votes were not enough to flip the seat.

